yu  knows this but apparently he does and so  asta will have plenty of time for his  wano training arc ryu also explains that  being shogun makes him something like  the wizard king of hino country which is  obviously an extremely prestigious  position however asta is surprised by  the fact that he doesn't seem to sense  any magical power coming from ryu and as  a result ryu really doesn't seem very  strong ryu readily admits that he isn't  really that strong which surprises both  asta and pretty much every person who is  reading this chapter after learning that  this dude is yami's childhood friend and  the shogun of hino country who somehow  knows everything that happened to asta  and who also somehow knows how exactly  asta got there i think we all just  assumed that this guy has some insane  and completely broken magic you know  some sort of tie magic or psychic magic  or prophecy magic something along those  lines but it seems like this guy doesn't  actually have any magic much like hosta  or at least that's what we've been led  to believe but i don't know if i buy it  yet that said the girl we met earlier is  not impressed with asta's suggestion  that ryu is not strong and so she tells  this gaijin asta to watch his mouth when  speaking to the shogun the girl's name  is revealed to be ichika and it's clear  that she has a great amount of respect  for you even though he allegedly isn't  that strong asta can tell right away  from ichika's ki that she is very angry  at him and although her key kind of  feels familiar he also knows that he  shouldn't go anywhere near her she is  clearly very strong and she is not a fan  of asta so he senses that he should stay  away ryu tells asta that he must be  shocked to just randomly wake up in  another country so he says that he will  show us to around in order to put his  mind at ease now this could just be me  but to me personally it would be more  reassuring if he actually explained how  exactly asta got here but instead 